":"genre","name":"Art Rock","n":1},{"id":55893123468232,"type":"genre","name":"Experimental Rock","n":1},{"id":31482837869539,"type":"genre","name":"Punk","n":1}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[{"id":181047479100421,"name":"Sonidos progresivos de los noventa","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1990,"end":2002,"desc":"Phish devuelven el rock alternativo a la radio y legitiman el regreso a la estética progresiva, sobre todo en la Costa Este: Blues Traveler, Motherhead Bug y Sulfur, Spin Doctors, Klezmatics, Cul De Sac (Ecim, China Gate) y Run On. El noise-punk-jazz de God Is My Co-pilot, Molecules, Love Child, Blowhole, Harry Pussy. Virginia como epicentro (Echolyn, Boud Deun, Rake, Dave Matthews Band). Solistas: Marc Ribot, Nicky Skopelitis, Buckethead, Loren Mazzacane, los zappianos Ant-Bee y Mike Keneally, Gary Lucas, Alan Licht, Bob Drake. En la Costa Oeste, Primus (Frizzle Fry), Mr Bungle, Amy Denio, Caveman Shoestore, Thessalonians. Internacional: Philharmonie, Xaal, Volapuk, Kevin Martin (God, Techno Animal, Ice, Bug). Y la Babel final: Bright, Meringue, Cerberus Shoal, Tin Hat Trio, Species Being.","color":"#38bdf8","family":"Progresivo, krautrock y jazz-rock","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#prog-90s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":30589811417482,"artist":"God Is My Co-pilot","artist_id":171177884251364,"title":"I Am Not This Body","year":1992,"ess":0,"yt":"Z01idxUvs20","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Sonidos progresivos de los noventa","scene_id":181047479100421,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#prog-90s","chapters":["Sección 6.2"],"pages":[[1,230,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":230,"text":"…never even dreamed of being. Still (1999), credited to Garner and Brown, was, de facto, a late addition to the Run On canon. Noise-punk-jazz 1992-95 God Is My Co-pilot (1) inherited Half Japanese's miniaturized dementia. I Am Not This Body (1992) packed 34 brief, childish, dissonant pieces that parodied all sorts…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":230,"text":"…Rat R guitarist Ron Anderson, had already done something similar on Steel Toe (1991). Ditto for Love Child in New York and their Witchcraft (1992). God Is My Co-pilot's idea was pursued by Spiny Anteaters in Canada, with the goofy, amateurish Last Supper (1998), Outhouse in Seattle, for example on Process Of…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":123366661637864,"type":"album","name":"Speed Yr Trip","list_id":110920763824306,"list":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Queercore","src":"musthear","rank":9,"year":1992,"note":null,"yt":"-s36S4ePPQ0","scaruffi":null},{"id":30589811417482,"type":"album","name":"I Am Not This Body","list_id":110920763824306,"list":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Queercore","src":"musthear","rank":11,"year":1992,"note":null,"yt":"QZmms25guuo","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":30589811417482,"type":"album","name":"I Am Not This Body","work_year":1992,"list_id":13018320481353,"list":"Scaruffi 1990s","src":"charts","rank":727,"year":1992,"note":null,"yt":"QZmms25guuo","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":107448635258989,"type":"album","name":"What Doctors Don’t Tell You","list_id":110920763824306,"list":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Queercore","src":"musthear","rank":36,"year":1993,"note":null,"yt":"Q74GK4QwyAw","scaruffi":null},{"id":230505075155728,"type":"album","name":"Straight Not","list_id":110920763824306,"list":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Queercore","src":"musthear","rank":71,"year":1993,"note":null,"yt":"4i7nuCXVNt0","scaruffi":null},{"id":57262627140783,"type":"album","name":"Getting Out of Boring Time Biting Into Boring Pie","list_id":110920763824306,"list":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Queercore","src":"musthear","rank"